-f 4	the -f/--factory flag takes no argument (bare -f starts the factory leader); a lane joins with -l or --lane, got "4"
-f worker	"worker" is the legacy role token; a lane joins with -l
-f lane-2	the -f/--factory flag takes no argument (bare -f starts the factory leader); a lane joins with -l or --lane, got "lane-2"
-f -a	the -a flag was removed; use -l (or --lane) to join the running factory as a lane (-f starts the leader)
-f -l	a launch carries at most one entry token; -f/--factory and -l/--lane are two entry tokens
-l -a	the -a flag was removed; use -l (or --lane) to join the running factory as a lane (-f starts the leader)
-l x	the -l/--lane flag takes no argument (it joins the running factory as the next free lane); --leader <name> selects the leader session
-l=x	the -l/--lane flag takes no argument (it joins the running factory as the next free lane); --leader <name> selects the leader session
-l --name foo	the -l/--lane flag already names the role; drop the --name/-n flag
-f --name lane-2	a --name lane-<n> value does not select a lane under -f/--factory (-f starts the factory leader); the lane entry is -l or --lane
-f --leader leader-2	the --leader flag names the leader session a lane join targets; it composes with -l or --lane only
--leader	the --leader flag requires a leader label
-l --leader lead-1	the --leader value "lead-1" is the legacy leader spelling; use "leader-1" (leader label forms: leader, leader-<n>, leader-<run-id>)
-l --clear-policy bogus	the --clear-policy flag takes clear-each, clear-when-full, or relaunch (got "bogus")
-f --no-auto-dispatch	the --no-auto-dispatch flag selects a lane's dispatch mode; the factory leader takes none
--agent	the --agent flag was removed; use -l (or --lane) to join the running factory as a lane (-f starts the leader)
--agent=x	the --agent flag was removed; use -l (or --lane) to join the running factory as a lane (-f starts the leader)
-- --agent x	the --agent flag was removed; use --lane (before any --) to join the running factory as a lane (-f starts the leader)
